# Copy to `.env`. Everything here is EXPO_PUBLIC_*, which means it is INLINED
# INTO THE JS BUNDLE at build time and recoverable from the installed app
# package. Nothing secret belongs in this file.

# Flashnet Orchestra — cross-chain swaps.
#
# MUST be a CLIENT key (fnp_…). Orchestra issues two kinds:
#
#   fnp_…  client key — public, scope-gated, meant to be embedded. Use this.
#   fn_…   server key — secret, FULL account access. Flashnet's own integration
#          guide says "never embed it in mobile or browser apps", and an
#          EXPO_PUBLIC_ value is embedded by definition.
#
# Get one from the Orchestra dashboard. `keyKind()` reports which sort is
# configured; a server key still WORKS, which is what makes it dangerous.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FLASHNET_API_KEY=fnp_replace_me

# Only needed for an ORIGIN-GATED client key — those answer 403
# `origin_required` on /quote and /submit until an Origin header is present.
# React Native's fetch is not a browser and sends none of its own. Any value is
# accepted unless the key has an allowlist, in which case use a registered one.
# Leave unset for a key without that restriction.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FLASHNET_ORIGIN=run.mercury.wallet

# NOTE on reading order status: a client key alone gets 403 `read_token_required`
# from /status. The per-order `readToken` comes back in the /quote response and
# is sent as a `?readToken=` QUERY PARAM alongside the key — not as a header,
# and not in place of it. The app persists it with each swap; see
# `Quote.readToken` in src/bridge/flashnet.ts.

# Garden Finance — TESTNET swaps.
#
# The wallet uses two swap providers, split by network, because neither covers
# both: Flashnet Orchestra has no test network at all (23 chains on its live
# route table, not one of them a testnet), and Garden has a full testnet catalog
# covering seven of the chains this wallet supports — Bitcoin testnet4 and Arc
# included.
#
# Get an app id from portal.garden.finance. Reads (/v2/chains, /v2/assets,
# /v2/quote) answer without one; order creation validates it, and an INVALID key
# is rejected with 401 while no key at all is allowed through — so a wrong value
# here fails louder than an empty one.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GARDEN_APP_ID=

# ── Network ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Which network the whole app runs on: `testnet` or `mainnet`. Unset falls back
# to DEFAULT_APP_ENVIRONMENT in src/lib/environment.ts.
#
# It is the DEFAULT, not a lock: the Networks screen can switch at runtime and
# that choice now survives a relaunch (see `chosen` in stores/networkStore.ts).
# This value is what a fresh install starts on.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ENVIRONMENT=testnet

# ── The hub ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One URL, three features — all of which are simply absent without it:
#
#   • Gateway mint relay   — instant sends. The app now REFUSES to burn when the
#                            hub is unreachable or its relayer is out of gas
#                            (`deliveryStatus`), so an unset value disables
#                            instant sends rather than stranding funds.
#   • Name sponsorship     — mercury usernames, paid for by the hub.
#   • The Graph index proxy — activity history and token discovery.
#
# The phone resolves this, not your Mac, so a LAN IP or a public origin — never
# `localhost`. The hub's own relayer key needs native gas on every destination
# chain it serves; check with GET /gateway/domains?environment=testnet.
EXPO_PUBLIC_RELAYER_URL=

# Stealth-payment transport. ONE CHARACTER different from the variable above and
# a completely different service — RELAY_URL is the stealth relay, RELAYER_URL
# is the hub. Unset falls back to the baked-in default in bridge/hubConfig.ts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RELAY_URL=

# ── Identity (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The ENS registry the wallet reads names from, and its parent name. Both
# default to the values compiled into the app.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENS_REGISTRY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ENS_PARENT=mercurywallet.eth
# EXPO_PUBLIC_REGISTRY_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_HUB_URL=

# ── Analytics (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset disables capture entirely.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# ── RPC overrides (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The public defaults are rate-limited, and a dropped read shows as an unknown
# balance rather than a wrong one — but the reads still cost time.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BTC_ESPLORA_MAINNET=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BTC_ESPLORA_MAINNET_FALLBACK=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_BTC_ESPLORA_TESTNET=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TOKEN_API_JWT=
